The licence of the resulting ffmpeg.exe
---------------------------------------

inside.sh configures FFmpeg with --enable-gpl --enable-version3 and links
libx264. It does NOT use --enable-nonfree: NVENC is reached through
nv-codec-headers and CUDA filters are compiled with clang (--enable-cuda-llvm),
neither of which needs nonfree. So the binary is licensed under the
GNU General Public License, version 3 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later), and may be
redistributed under those terms. `ffmpeg.exe -L` prints the same.

